+age-of-consent | 1891-03-19 | Kolkata | women, power | all | Age of Consent Act, 1891 | The Age of Consent Act | The Age of Consent Act, enacted in British India on 19 March 1891, raised the age of consent for all girls, married or unmarried, from ten to twelve years. | In 1891 a law raised the age of consent for girls from ten to twelve.
+swadeshi | 1905-08-07 | Kolkata | trade, work, power | east | Swadeshi movement | The Swadeshi movement begins | The Swadeshi movement was a self-sufficiency movement within the Indian independence movement. In response to the plan to partition Bengal, it was formally started from the Town Hall at Calcutta on 7 August 1905, to curb foreign goods by relying on domestic production. | When the British planned to divide Bengal, people protested by turning away from foreign goods and using things made in India instead.
