+vaikom | 1924-03-30..1925-11-23 | Vaikom | religion, power | south | Vaikom Satyagraha | The Vaikom Satyagraha | The Vaikom Satyagraha, from 30 March 1924 to 23 November 1925, was a nonviolent agitation for access to the prohibited public roads around the Vaikom Temple in the Kingdom of Travancore. | For more than a year people in Kerala protested peacefully so that everyone could use the public roads around a temple.
+self-respect | 1925 | Tamil Nadu | power, religion, women | south | Self-Respect Movement | The Self-Respect Movement | The Self-Respect Movement, founded in 1925 in South India and led in Tamil Nadu by E. V. Ramasamy, known as Periyar, aimed at social equality for those oppressed by the caste system. | In 1925 a movement began in southern India that told people of every caste to respect themselves and demand to be treated as equals.
