+sarda-act | 1929-09-28 | New Delhi | women, power | all | Child Marriage Restraint Act, 1929 | The Child Marriage Restraint Act | The Child Marriage Restraint Act, passed on 28 September 1929, fixed the minimum age of marriage at 14 years for girls and 18 for boys. | In 1929 a law said that girls could not be married before they were 14, or boys before 18.
