+poona-pact | 1932-09 | Pune | power | deccan | Poona Pact | The Poona Pact | The Poona Pact of September 1932 was a negotiated settlement between Mahatma Gandhi and B. R. Ambedkar that increased the political representation of the depressed classes, now known as Scheduled Castes. | In 1932 Gandhi and Ambedkar made an agreement that gave more seats in the law-making councils to people of the lowest castes.
