+first-election | 1951-10-25..1952-02-21 | New Delhi | power | all | 1951–52 Indian general election | India's first general election | India's first national elections after independence were held between 25 October 1951 and 21 February 1952. Voters elected 489 members of the first Lok Sabha. | In 1951 and 1952 the people of India voted for their own government for the first time.
+sreeramulu | 1952 | Chennai | language, power | south | Potti Sreeramulu | A fast for a Telugu state | Potti Sreeramulu undertook a 58-day hunger strike in 1952, demanding a separate state for Telugu-speaking people from the Madras Presidency. He is remembered for his role in the creation of Andhra State. | In 1952 Potti Sreeramulu refused to eat for 58 days to demand a state for people who speak Telugu.
+hindu-code | 1950s | New Delhi | women, power | all | Hindu code bills | The Hindu code bills | The Hindu code bills were several laws passed in the 1950s that aimed to codify and reform Hindu personal law, including the Hindu Marriage Act and the Hindu Succession Act. | In the 1950s new laws changed the rules about marriage and inheriting property for Hindus.
