+chipko | 1970s | India | nature, women, power | all | Chipko movement | The Chipko movement | The Chipko movement is a forest conservation movement in which protesters in the 1970s hugged trees to stop commercial logging. Women took a large part, being the ones most affected by deforestation. In 1987 it received the Right Livelihood Award. | In the 1970s villagers, many of them women, protected their forests by hugging the trees so that they could not be cut down.
+kesavananda | 1970s | New Delhi | power | all | Kesavananda Bharati v. State of Kerala | The basic structure judgement | Kesavananda Bharati v. State of Kerala, a case filed in 1970, was a landmark decision of the Supreme Court of India that outlined the basic structure doctrine of the Constitution. By 7 judges to 6 the court asserted its right to strike down amendments that violate it. | In a famous case, India's highest court decided that some basic parts of the Constitution can never be removed.
+emergency | 1975..1977 | New Delhi | power | all | The Emergency (India) | The Emergency | The Emergency was a 21-month period from 1975 to 1977 when Prime Minister Indira Gandhi declared a state of emergency across India, citing internal and external threats. | From 1975 to 1977 the Prime Minister, Indira Gandhi, ruled with special emergency powers.
+mandal | 1979 | New Delhi | power | all | Mandal Commission | The Mandal Commission | The Mandal Commission, or Socially and Educationally Backward Classes Commission, was established in 1979 by the Janata Party government under Prime Minister Morarji Desai. | In 1979 the government set up a commission to find out which groups of people had been left behind and needed help.
+bhopal | 1984-12-03 | Bhopal disaster | nature, work, medicine | central | Bhopal disaster | The Bhopal gas disaster | On 3 December 1984 over 500,000 people near the Union Carbide pesticide plant in Bhopal, Madhya Pradesh, were exposed to the highly toxic gas methyl isocyanate. | On 3 December 1984 poisonous gas leaked from a factory in Bhopal. More than half a million people breathed it in.
+narmada-bachao | 1985 | Sardar Sarovar Dam | nature, power, movement | west | Narmada Bachao Andolan | Narmada Bachao Andolan | Narmada Bachao Andolan is a social movement founded by Medha Patkar in 1985, organising tribes, farmers and environmentalists against a number of large dam projects on the Narmada. | In 1985 Medha Patkar started a movement of villagers and farmers against the big dams being built on the Narmada River.
