+vishaka | 1997 | New Delhi | women, work | all | Vishakha and Others v. State of Rajasthan | The Vishaka case | Vishaka v. State of Rajasthan was a 1997 Supreme Court case brought by women's groups after Bhanwari Devi, a social worker in Rajasthan, was attacked for stopping a child marriage. The court drew on the guarantee of gender equality and the right to work with human dignity. | In 1997 women's groups went to India's highest court after a social worker was attacked for stopping a child marriage. The court spoke up for women's right to work in safety and dignity.
+rti | 2005 | New Delhi | power | all | Right to Information Act, 2005 | The Right to Information Act | The Right to Information Act of 2005 sets out the rules and procedures for citizens' right to access information from the government. | Since 2005 a law has let any citizen ask the government for information.
+nrega | 2005-08-23 | New Delhi | work, power | all | Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Act, 2005 | A right to work | The Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Act, passed on 23 August 2005, is a social welfare measure that aimed to guarantee the "right to work". | In 2005 a law promised paid work each year to families in the countryside who need it.
+navtej | 2018-09-06 | New Delhi | power | all | Navtej Singh Johar v. Union of India | Section 377 is struck down | On 6 September 2018 the Supreme Court of India unanimously decriminalised all consensual sex among adults, including homosexual sex. | In 2018 India's highest court ruled that the law may not punish adults for whom they love.
